{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c539","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07aa8-9772-7fb3-a3d6-487c1d889dad"},"sequence":247,"recorded_at":1780531400000489,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"30b54554-a36a-471e-9a51-ed21081d308f"},"task_id":"30b54554-a36a-471e-9a51-ed21081d308f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"30b54554-a36a-471e-9a51-ed21081d308f","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/r3-outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260906-2okwyf round 3 — F2 instrument: outcome\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (handed off to review; review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n4|\n5|Candidate tree: `34b88fb9bb6e9fe050e400d6b51685e9cbd6547b`\n6|(verified: detached index — `GIT_INDEX_FILE` copy + `read-tree HEAD` +\n7|`add -A` + `write-tree` — worktree index untouched, HEAD stays at the\n8|`114a056` checkpoint, change uncommitted. All 5 key paths in-tree with\n9|`git hash-object` byte-equal to the tree blob, 5/5 MATCH, including the\n10|two untracked test files. Computed AFTER every tracked write, including\n11|the LOGBOOK append. The Change Request record is the orchestrator's\n12|integration step; this OID is the candidate it must carry.)\n13|\n14|Round-3 scope (3 code/test paths + LOGBOOK; round-1/round-2 files untouched):\n15|\n16|- `internal/terminalbackend/manifest.go` — `Reconcile` validates both\n17|  `manifest.TerminalBackendID` (manifest.go:1696) and\n18|  `probe.TerminalBackendID` (manifest.go:1699) through `ParseID` before\n19|  any check runs.\n20|- `internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go` — `ParseID` comment\n21|  rewritten (false package-wide universal replaced by a pointer to the\n22|  instrument; terminalbackend.go:163).\n23|- `internal/terminalbackend/backend_id_entry_census_test.go` — NEW: the\n24|  (site, reaching exported entry) census instrument (TestBackendIDEntryCensus).\n25|- `LOGBOOK.md` — this round's entry (newest first).\n26|\n27|## 1. F2 — Reconcile entry gate (fixed, not named)\n28|\n29|Pre-fix reproduction, driven through the production entry point\n30|`terminalbackend.Reconcile` with `200x\"A\" + ESC[31m + ../../etc/passwd`\n31|(221 bytes, grammar- and bound-refused) as equal hostile IDs:\n32|\n33|- differing digests → `manifest.go` substitution refusal, 305 bytes,\n34|  `contains(hostile)==true`, `BackendID` carries the full string;\n35|- matching digests, foreign generation digest → generation refusal,\n36|  313 bytes, `contains(hostile)==true`.\n37|\n38|Both are the defect A9 named at `ParseID`, live at the sibling that\n39|never calls it. Fix: entry validation through `ParseID` for both IDs\n40|(the pattern `CheckVersionTuple` and `CheckProviderDescriptor` already\n41|use). A refused ID returns the `ParseID` refusal — whose bound and\n42|grammar arms carry no `BackendID` — and never reaches the naming arms.\n43|\n44|- Red-before (unfixed code): new census `reconcile` battery FAILs —\n45|  both hostile shapes at both arms (305/313B echoes), plus the short\n46|  shape at 111/119B.\n47|- Green-after: `TestBackendIDEntryCensus` PASS, exit 0, log line\n48|  `backend-id entry census: 41/41 pairs validated, 1 site exemptions\n49|  plus 1 pair exemptions pinned`.\n50|\n51|## 2. F2 — the instrument (what closes the class)\n52|\n53|`TestBackendIDEntryCensus` (internal package: reuses `deriveRefusalArms`\n54|filtered to `BackendID:` constructions, `invcore.MustScanProduction`\n55|for entry coverage, and the shared runtime refusal recorder for fire\n56|attribution — no new file walker):\n57|\n58|- Denominator derived, not listed: 31 BackendID sites (30 refused\n59|  through pairs + 1 exempt) and every exported entry (58 derived:\n60|  10 pair entries + 5 hostile-only + 43 free with r