BOOK.md` — this round's entry (newest first).\n26|\n27|## 1. F2 — Reconcile entry gate (fixed, not named)\n28|\n29|Pre-fix reproduction, driven through the production entry point\n30|`terminalbackend.Reconcile` with `200x\"A\" + ESC[31m + ../../etc/passwd`\n31|(221 bytes, grammar- and bound-refused) as equal hostile IDs:\n32|\n33|- differing digests → `manifest.go` substitution refusal, 305 bytes,\n34|  `contains(hostile)==true`, `BackendID` carries the full string;\n35|- matching digests, foreign generation digest → generation refusal,\n36|  313 bytes, `contains(hostile)==true`.\n37|\n38|Both are the defect A9 named at `ParseID`, live at the sibling that\n39|never calls it. Fix: entry validation through `ParseID` for both IDs\n40|(the pattern `CheckVersionTuple` and `CheckProviderDescriptor` already\n41|use). A refused ID returns the `ParseID` refusal — whose bound and\n42|grammar arms carry no `BackendID` — and never reaches the naming arms.\n43|\n44|- Red-before (unfixed code): new census `reconcile` battery FAILs —\n45|  both hostile shapes at both arms (305/313B echoes), plus the short\n46|  shape at 111/119B.\n47|- Green-after: `TestBackendIDEntryCensus` PASS, exit 0, log line\n48|  `backend-id entry census: 41/41 pairs validated, 1 site exemptions\n49|  plus 1 pair exemptions pinned`.\n50|\n51|## 2. F2 — the instrument (what closes the class)\n52|\n53|`TestBackendIDEntryCensus` (internal package: reuses `deriveRefusalArms`\n54|filtered to `BackendID:` constructions, `invcore.MustScanProduction`\n55|for entry coverage, and the shared runtime refusal recorder for fire\n56|attribution — no new file walker):\n57|\n58|- Denominator derived, not listed: 31 BackendID sites (30 refused\n59|  through pairs + 1 exempt) and every exported entry (58 derived:\n60|  10 pair entries + 5 hostile-only + 43 free with reasons).\n61|- 41 (site, entry) pairs. A site reachable through two entries appears\n62|  twice — collapsing those rows was the bug. Every pair states its\n63|  guard; every pair is proved twice: hostile battery through its entry\n64|  (2 shapes, `BackendID == \"\"` and `!Contains(Error(), hostile)`) and\n65|  a validated fire (12 own fires with recorder line-attribution + 29\n66|  inventoried-witness citations resolved mechanically against\n67|  `DeclaredArmIdentities`: row present, same entry, not bound).\n68|- Exemptions executed, not asserted: digest-null site (direct\n69|  `validate()` pin in-file) and the shadowed digest-parse/Admit pair\n70|  (malformed digest refuses at the parse arm — the shadow proof).\n71|- Ratio produced by the test (see log line above), both directions\n72|  checked (unregistered site, orphan row, unlisted entry all fail).\n73|\n74|Control plant C1 (reviewer's ready-made vector: ParseID guard deleted\n75|from `CheckProviderDescriptor`): the new test FAILs with the exact\n76|308-byte echo while the rest of the package suite stays green\n77|(`--- FAIL: TestBackendIDEntryCensus` is the only failure) —\n78|reproducing the finding that the old suite holds none of this class.\n79|\n80|## 3. Non-blocking notes closed\n81|\n82|- N1 (anchors never re-derived): all anchors above re-derived on the\n83|  final tree after the last artifact write — Reconcile guards\n84|  manifest.go:1696/1699, naming sites :1741/:1777/:2099/:2102,\n85|  descriptor guard terminalbackend.go:646, ParseID census note :163.\n86|- N2 (ordering filed as narrowing): `R-tb-checktuple-order` is filed\n87|  `ordering` in this round's battery (class list below); the rev-1/2\n88|  mislabel is superseded, not repeated.\n89|\n90|## 4. Mutation battery (round 3, this tree)\n91|\n92|Harness: same verdict semantics (`KILLED` = mask exit != 0;\n93|byte-for-byte restore verified by the harness, tree verified clean\n94|after). Masks non-empty and verified by `-list` semantics (ran counts\n95|below): inventory-census 15 ran, behav 273 ran (r2's 11 + the new\n96|census test), audit full-package 695 ran. Full bodies in\n97|`TASK-260906-2okwyf_battery-r3.json` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_mutants-r3.json`.\n98|\n99|| mutant | class | what it narrows the gate to | named test that fails | verdict / killers |\n100||---|---|---|---|---|\n101|| N-tb-reconcile-lengthgated: entry checks run only when `len > maxIDBytes` | narrowing | admits exactly the grammar-refused-but-bounded subclass (len27 echoes, len221 still refused) | `TestBackendIDEntryCensus/reconcile/len27` (len221 rows pass — narrowing proven off the subtests) | KILLED / behav (census 15 SURVIVED) |\n102|| D-tb-reconcile-entry: both entry blocks deleted | arm-deletion | gate absent; all hostile IDs echo at the naming arms | `TestBackendIDEntryCensus/reconcile` (both shapes, both arms) | KILLED / behav (census SURVIVED — entry calls are not refuse lines) |\n103|| D-tb-checkdesc-entry: entry block deleted (= C1) | arm-deletion | gate absent; hostile descriptor IDs echo (308B) | `TestBackendIDEntryCensus/check-provider-descriptor` | KILLED / behav (census SURVIVED; rest of package green) |\n104|| R-tb-checktuple-order: entry check moved after the version arms | ordering | validation present but bypassed on every version-failure path | `TestBackendIDEntryCensus/check-version-tuple` + `TestCheckVersionTupleRefusesHostileBackendIDWithoutEcho` | KILLED / behav (census SURVIVED — same lines, moved) |\n105|| C-tb-reconcile-deadarm: unreachable new BackendID arm in Reconcile (space can never pass the entry) | census-only | — (no behavior change) | inventory `TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllDeclared` + entry-census mapping inside behav | KILLED / census + behav-mapping (no behavioral probe observes it) |\n106|| S-tb-statusresult-shadow: occurrence-1 condition widened to subsume occurrence-2 inputs (lines unchanged) | audit-only | — (occurrence-2 witness proves its pair through the sibling) | full-run audit naming `conformance.go:765` | KILLED / audit only (census 15 + behav 273 SURVIVED) |\n107|| X-control-notapplied | control | — | — | NOT_APPLIED (anchor occurs 0 times) |\n108|| X-control-compilefail | control | — | — | COMPILE_FAIL (`go vet` syntax error, provider.go) |\n109|\n110|Killed over applied: 6/6 killed, 0 survived. No surviving mutant, so no\n111|survival bounds to state. NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL are distinct\n112|control rows, not in the denominator.\n113|\n114|## 5. Gates (real exit codes, standalone processes)\n115|\n116|- `go test ./internal/terminalbackend/ -run TestBackendIDEntryCensus`\n117|  pre-fix: FAIL (reconcile battery, 305/313B echoes).\n118|- `go test ./... -count=1`: exit 0 — 23 ok, 0 FAIL.\n119|- `go test -race ./internal/terminalbackend/ -count=1`: exit 0.\n120|- `go test -cover` tb/ph/pv: exit 0 (95.4% / 86.0% / 97.8%).\n121|- `go vet ./...`: exit 0. `gofmt -l internal/`: clean.\n122|- `GOOS=windows go build ./...`: exit 0.\n123|\n124|## 6. AC coverage\n125|\n126|4 of 4 rows driven, each with a named test (round-1/2 rows re-verified\n127|green this round; F2 is the previously-missing entry-dimension row):\n128|\n129|| AC row | production call site | driving test |\n130||---|---|---|\n131|| two literals equal directly, either side alone reddens, SPEC-independent | `provider.Builtins()` / `provhost.profileProviders` | `TestBuiltinsEqualProfileProviders` (re-ran PASS) |\n132|| §6.5 vs §7.1 asymmetry cited at both sites, or decision recorded | `terminalbackend.DigestFile`, `provider.trustCandidate` | citation pair, unchanged since rev 1 |\n133|| `ParseID` prints no unbounded refused input | `terminalbackend.ParseID` + every ID entry | `TestParseIDGrammarRefusalEchoesNothing` + census hostile batteries (15 entries × 2 shapes) |\n134|| every closed nit has a fail-before test; every open nit a stated bound | `Reconcile` entry, `decodeValidatedProbe`, `parseMajor` | census (red-before above), `TestDecodeValidatedProbeHandsUsableMembersToRequireCapability`, `TestParseMajorLeadingZeroIsClassifiedAsForeign` (all re-ran PASS) |\n135|\n136|Round-1/round-2 outcome and battery resources stand for the unchanged\n137|regions; all named pins re-ran green on this tree (see §5).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
