{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07aa8-9772-7fb3-a3d6-487c1d889dad"},"sequence":315,"recorded_at":1780531400000625,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b"},"call_id":"call_01a07aa9a50275e0a6f9ef08c1c630f6","text":"Read text file `internal/terminalbackend/backend_id_entry_census_test.go`.\n1|// BackendID entry census: every BackendID-carrying refusal reaches its\n2|// refusal with an identity that passed ParseID or mustParseID.\n3|//\n4|// The failure this file exists to prevent: a package-wide comment asserting\n5|// that every BackendID named in a refusal is a validated identity, while a\n6|// hostile identity driven through a second exported entry renders verbatim\n7|// into a refusal. It happened twice in a row: first CheckVersionTuple named\n8|// an unvalidated parameter at three arms, then Reconcile named unvalidated\n9|// struct members at two arms (manifest.go checkProbeIdentity executable\n10|// substitution and checkProbeGeneration probe generation binding), while the\n11|// site-keyed census read 31/31 validated. The census unit was the site; the\n12|// property is per entry path: those two arms are validated via AdmitProbe\n13|// (which parses both documents) and unvalidated via Reconcile (which takes\n14|// both structs directly). A site-keyed table records the safe path and\n15|// drops the unsafe one, so no corrected row count can make it true.\n16|//\n17|// This census is keyed by (site, reaching exported entry). Every pair\n18|// either reaches its refusal with an identity that passed ParseID or\n19|// mustParseID, or is a declared exemption with a reason. The ratio the\n20|// outcome reports is produced below (TestBackendIDEntryCensus logs\n21|// validated/total), not read off this table: the table is checked in both\n22|// directions against the production derivation, and every pair carries an\n23|// executed proof in this test.\n24|//\n25|// What each pair's proof is, by kind:\n26|//\n27|//   - hostile-noecho: driving a grammar- or bound-refused identity through\n28|//     the pair's entry refuses at the ParseID/mustParseID guard (or at a\n29|//     document-membership gate for raw-document entries) with BackendID\n30|//     empty and the refused bytes absent from Error(). Deleting the guard\n31|//     (control plant C1: the ParseID check out of CheckProviderDescriptor)\n32|//     reopens a 308-byte echo and fails the entry battery.\n33|//   - validated-fire: driving a grammar-valid identity that fails the\n34|//     pair's own rule fires the pair's site (attributed through the\n35|//     runtime refusal recorder) with BackendID equal to that validated\n36|//     identity. Multi-entry sites carry one fire per entry; single-entry\n37|//     sites cite their inventoried executed witness, which this test\n38|//     resolves mechanically against DeclaredArmIdentities (row present,\n39|//     same entry, not bound) rather than by reading.\n40|//\n41|// Derivation reuses the package inventory (deriveRefusalArms) filtered to\n42|// constructions naming BackendID, plus invcore production scanning for\n43|// exported-entry coverage. No new file walker: the site set is the\n44|// inventory's, and attribution is the shared runtime recorder's.\n45|//\n46|// Stated bounds (not inferred):\n47|//   - ParseID's own reserved-namespace arm names its input by design: the\n48|//     input passed the bound and grammar gates first, so the echo is a\n49|//     validated identity, never raw input. It is a pair, not an\n50|//     exemption, proved by the reserved fire below.\n51|//   - Registration.validate's \"executable_digest must be null\" arm is\n52|//     unreachable through any exported entry (RegisterExternal's kind\n53|//     gate admits exactly the digest-carrying kinds; New builds builtins\n54|//     without digests). It is the single exempt site, pinned white-box\n55|//     by TestValidateRefusesBuiltinKindWithDigest.\n56|//   - Error predicates, platform defaults, ledger, conformance and\n57|//     descriptor-projection entries take no backend-identity input or\n58|//     emit no BackendID refusal; each is listed in backendIDFreeEntries\n59|//     with its reason, and the entry-coverage check fails closed on any\n60|//     entry missing from both lists.\n61|package terminalbackend\n62|\n63|import (\n64|\t\"crypto/sha256\"\n65|\t\"encoding/hex\"\n66|\t\"encoding/json\"\n67|\t\"errors\"\n68|\t\"go/ast\"\n69|\t\"strconv\"\n70|\t\"strings\"\n71|\t\"testing\"\n72|\t\"time\"\n73|\n74|\t\"github.com/gowebpki/jcs\"\n75|\n76|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/invcore\"\n77|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n78|)\n79|\n80|// backendIDHostileLong is over the 128-byte bound and grammar-refused:\n81|// terminal escapes plus traversal content, the shape the F2 finding drove\n82|// through Reconcile (221 bytes).\n83|var backendIDHostileLong = strings.Repeat(\"A\", 200) + \"\\x1b[31m\" + \"../../etc/passwd\"\n84|\n85|// backendIDHostileShort is within the bound but grammar-refused (27 bytes):\n86|// the subclass a length-gated entry check would admit.\n87|const backendIDHostileShort = \"BAD ID\\x1b[31m../../etc/passwd\"\n88|\n89|// backendIDValid is a grammar-valid third-party identity used as the\n90|// validated control wherever a fire must name its identity.\n91|const backendIDValid = \"com.example.term\"\n92|\n93|// backendIDPair is one (BackendID-carrying refusal site, reaching exported\n94|// entry) census unit. Site fields use the inventory key space (file,\n95|// receiver-qualified function, code symbol, static detail, occurrence\n96|// within that key); entry uses the inventory entry spelling\n97|// (\"CheckProviderDescriptor\", \"Reconcile\", \"AdmitProbe\").\n98|// guard states the validation mechanism in prose; fire cites the proof\n99|// that the site fires with a validated identity (\"witness:<entry>\" for an\n100|// inventoried executed witness at that entry, \"census:<probe>\" for a\n101|// validated fire driven in this file).\n102|type backendIDPair struct {\n103|\tfile       string\n104|\tfunction   string\n105|\tcode       string\n106|\tdetail     string\n107|\toccurrence int\n108|\tentry      string\n109|\tguard      string\n110|\tfire       string\n111|}\n112|\n113|// backendIDPairs is the full (site, entry) census. A site reachable\n114|// through two exported entries appears twice; collapsing those rows is\n115|// the exact failure this census exists to prevent.\n116|var backendIDPairs = []backendIDPair{\n117|\t// ParseID trust root: the reserved arm names only grammar-valid input.\n118|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"ParseID\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"terminal_backend_id reserved namespace\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"ParseID\", guard: \"input passed the bound and grammar gates in this function before the echo\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/reserved-names-validated-identity\"},\n119|\n120|\t// Registration.validate: mustParseID(record.ID) at the validate top.\n121|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registration.validate\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"implementation_version semver\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(record.ID) at validate top; observed is caller-bound to the validated trust entry\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n122|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registration.validate\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: passthroughDetail, occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(record.ID) at validate top; funneled platform details name the validated record\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n123|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registration.validate\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"executable_digest\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(record.ID) at validate top\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n124|\n125|\t// validateProtocolVersions through New: the only caller-supplied member\n126|\t// is the version list; the identity is the BuiltinTmux constant.\n127|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"validateProtocolVersions\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"protocol_versions bound\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"New\", guard: \"BuiltinTmux constant; census proves ParseID(BuiltinTmux) admits\", fire: \"witness:New\"},\n128|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"validateProtocolVersions\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"protocol_versions major 1\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"New\", guard: \"BuiltinTmux constant; census proves ParseID(BuiltinTmux) admits\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/protocol-major-1-via-New\"},\n129|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"validateProtocolVersions\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"protocol_versions sorted unique\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"New\", guard: \"BuiltinTmux constant; census proves ParseID(BuiltinTmux) admits\", fire: \"witness:New\"},\n130|\t// validateProtocolVersions through RegisterExternal: record.ID passed\n131|\t// mustParseID at the validate top before the version call.\n132|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"validateProtocolVersions\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"protocol_versions bound\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(record.ID) at validate top before the version call\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/protocol-bound-via-RegisterExternal\"},\n133|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"validateProtocolVersions\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"protocol_versions major 1\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(record.ID) at validate top before the version call\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n134|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"validateProtocolVersions\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"protocol_versions sorted unique\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(record.ID) at validate top before the version call\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/protocol-order-via-RegisterExternal\"},\n135|\n136|\t// TrustEntry.validate: mustParseID(entry.BackendID) at the validate top.\n137|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"TrustEntry.validate\", code: \"CodeAmbiguous\", detail: \"external_trust reserved namespace\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(entry.BackendID) at validate top\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n138|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"TrustEntry.validate\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"external_trust executable_path\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(entry.BackendID) at validate top\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n139|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"TrustEntry.validate\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"external_trust executable_digest\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"mustParseID(entry.BackendID) at validate top\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n140|\n141|\t// Registry.RegisterExternal: entry.validate then the identity binding\n142|\t// (observed.ID must equal the validated entry ID) then\n143|\t// observed.validate, so every arm below names a validated identity.\n144|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.RegisterExternal\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"external_trust disabled\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"entry.validate (mustParseID) before the enabled gate\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n145|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.RegisterExternal\", code: \"CodeAmbiguous\", detail: \"external_trust identity binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"entry.validate (mustParseID); the arm names the validated entry ID\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n146|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.RegisterExternal\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"external implementation_kind\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"entry.validate (mustParseID); the arm names the validated entry ID\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n147|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.RegisterExternal\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"executable substitution\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"entry.validate plus observed.validate plus the identity binding before the digest compare\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n148|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.RegisterExternal\", code: \"CodeAmbiguous\", detail: \"duplicate backend_id\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"observed.validate (mustParseID) before the store compare\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n149|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.RegisterExternal\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"implementation drift\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RegisterExternal\", guard: \"observed.validate (mustParseID) before the store compare\", fire: \"witness:RegisterExternal\"},\n150|\n151|\t// Registry.Resolve: ParseID at the entry; the arm names the admitted ID.\n152|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.Resolve\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"unregistered terminal_backend_id\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"Resolve\", guard: \"ParseID(backendID) at the entry\", fire: \"witness:Resolve\"},\n153|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.Resolve\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"unregistered terminal_backend_id\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RequireRestoreBinding\", guard: \"ParseID(boundBackendID) at the entry before Resolve re-validates\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/unregistered-via-RequireRestoreBinding\"},\n154|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.Resolve\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"unregistered terminal_backend_id\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProbe\", guard: \"ParseManifest admission (ParseID) then Resolve re-validation\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/unregistered-via-AdmitProbe\"},\n155|\n156|\t// Registry.RequireRestoreBinding: both IDs pass ParseID at the entry.\n157|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registry.RequireRestoreBinding\", code: \"CodeRestoreMismatch\", detail: \"restore requires the prior binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"RequireRestoreBinding\", guard: \"ParseID(candidateBackendID) at the entry; the arm names the validated candidate\", fire: \"witness:RequireRestoreBinding\"},\n158|\n159|\t// CheckVersionTuple: ParseID at the entry (this task's round-2 fix).\n160|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckVersionTuple\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"implementation_version semver\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"CheckVersionTuple\", guard: \"ParseID(backendID) at the entry before any version arm\", fire: \"witness:CheckVersionTuple\"},\n161|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckVersionTuple\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"protocol_version major 1\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"CheckVersionTuple\", guard: \"ParseID(backendID) at the entry before any version arm\", fire: \"witness:CheckVersionTuple\"},\n162|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckVersionTuple\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"protocol_version membership\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"CheckVersionTuple\", guard: \"ParseID(backendID) at the entry before any version arm\", fire: \"witness:CheckVersionTuple\"},\n163|\n164|\t// CheckProviderDescriptor: ParseID(descriptor.BackendID) at the entry;\n165|\t// every arm below names that validated descriptor ID, never the binding.\n166|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"descriptor backend binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseID(descriptor.BackendID) at the entry\", fire: \"witness:CheckProviderDescriptor\"},\n167|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"descriptor binding digest\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseID(descriptor.BackendID) at the entry\", fire: \"witness:CheckProviderDescriptor\"},\n168|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"descriptor binding digest\", occurrence: 2, entry: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseID(descriptor.BackendID) at the entry\", fire: \"witness:CheckProviderDescriptor\"},\n169|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"descriptor version binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseID(descriptor.BackendID) at the entry\", fire: \"witness:CheckProviderDescriptor\"},\n170|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeStaleGeneration\", detail: \"descriptor generation binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseID(descriptor.BackendID) at the entry\", fire: \"witness:CheckProviderDescriptor\"},\n171|\t// CheckProviderDescriptor through AdmitProviderDescriptor: the document\n172|\t// admission validates the ID (ParseID at descriptor.go ParseProvider-\n173|\t// Descriptor) and CheckProviderDescriptor re-validates the projection.\n174|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"descriptor backend binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseProviderDescriptor admission (ParseID) plus CheckProviderDescriptor re-validation\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/descriptor-backend-via-AdmitProviderDescriptor\"},\n175|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"descriptor binding digest\", occurrence: 2, entry: \"AdmitProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseProviderDescriptor admission (ParseID) plus CheckProviderDescriptor re-validation\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/descriptor-digest-mismatch-via-AdmitProviderDescriptor\"},\n176|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"descriptor version binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseProviderDescriptor admission (ParseID) plus CheckProviderDescriptor re-validation\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/descriptor-version-via-AdmitProviderDescriptor\"},\n177|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeStaleGeneration\", detail: \"descriptor generation binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProviderDescriptor\", guard: \"ParseProviderDescriptor admission (ParseID) plus CheckProviderDescriptor re-validation\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/descriptor-generation-via-AdmitProviderDescriptor\"},\n178|\n179|\t// checkProbeIdentity executable substitution: validated via AdmitProbe\n180|\t// (ParseProbe admission) and, since this task, at the Reconcile entry.\n181|\t{file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"checkProbeIdentity\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"executable substitution\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProbe\", guard: \"ParseProbe admission (ParseID) then Reconcile entry re-validation\", fire: \"witness:AdmitProbe\"},\n182|\t{file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"checkProbeIdentity\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"executable substitution\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"Reconcile\", guard: \"ParseID(manifest.TerminalBackendID) and ParseID(probe.TerminalBackendID) at the Reconcile entry\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/substitution-via-Reconcile\"},\n183|\t// checkProbeGeneration probe generation binding: same two entries.\n184|\t{file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"checkProbeGeneration\", code: \"CodeStaleGeneration\", detail: \"probe generation binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"Reconcile\", guard: \"ParseID(probe.TerminalBackendID) at the Reconcile entry\", fire: \"witness:Reconcile\"},\n185|\t{file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"checkProbeGeneration\", code: \"CodeStaleGeneration\", detail: \"probe generation binding\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProbe\", guard: \"ParseProbe admission (ParseID) then Reconcile entry re-validation\", fire: \"census:TestBackendIDEntryCensus/generation-via-AdmitProbe\"},\n186|\n187|\t// checkManifestRecordBinding: AdmitProbe-only; the manifest ID passed\n188|\t// ParseManifest admission (ParseID) and Resolve re-validation.\n189|\t{file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"checkManifestRecordBinding\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"manifest implementation drift\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProbe\", guard: \"ParseManifest admission (ParseID) plus Resolve re-validation\", fire: \"witness:AdmitProbe\"},\n190|\t{file: \"manifest.go\", function: \"checkManifestRecordBinding\", code: \"CodeUntrusted\", detail: \"executable substitution\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProbe\", guard: \"ParseManifest admission (ParseID) plus Resolve re-validation\", fire: \"witness:AdmitProbe\"},\n191|}\n192|\n193|// backendIDExemptSites names derived BackendID sites with no (site, entry)\n194|// pair because no exported entry can reach them. Each carries the reason\n195|// and the pinning test; the derivation check below requires every derived\n196|// BackendID site to appear either here or in backendIDPairs.\n197|var backendIDExemptSites = []struct {\n198|\tfile       string\n199|\tfunction   string\n200|\tcode       string\n201|\tdetail     string\n202|\toccurrence int\n203|\treason     string\n204|\tpin        string\n205|}{\n206|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"Registration.validate\", code: \"CodeDrift\", detail: \"executable_digest must be null\", occurrence: 1, reason: boundUnreachableDigestNull, pin: \"TestValidateRefusesBuiltinKindWithDigest\"},\n207|}\n208|\n209|// backendIDExemptPairs names (site, entry) combinations with no reaching\n210|// input, each with the reason and the pin this file executes. Unlike\n211|// backendIDExemptSites (no entry reaches the site at all), the site here\n212|// is reachable through other entries; only the listed entry cannot\n213|// deliver an input to it.\n214|var backendIDExemptPairs = []struct {\n215|\tfile       string\n216|\tfunction   string\n217|\tcode       string\n218|\tdetail     string\n219|\toccurrence int\n220|\tentry      string\n221|\treason     string\n222|}{\n223|\t// CheckProviderDescriptor's digest-parse arm (occurrence 1) through\n224|\t// AdmitProviderDescriptor: ParseProviderDescriptor refuses a\n225|\t// malformed binding digest at its own \"descriptor digest\" arm before\n226|\t// any comparison runs, so only a well-formed digest reaches the\n227|\t// match, and a well-formed digest passes the parse arm. The digest\n228|\t// mismatch arm (occurrence 2) stays a live pair. The pin below drives\n229|\t// a malformed digest through AdmitProviderDescriptor and requires\n230|\t// the parse arm, proving the shadow.\n231|\t{file: \"terminalbackend.go\", function: \"CheckProviderDescriptor\", code: \"CodeNotFound\", detail: \"descriptor binding digest\", occurrence: 1, entry: \"AdmitProviderDescriptor\", reason: \"shadowed: ParseProviderDescriptor descriptor-digest arm fires first on any malformed digest\"},\n232|}\n233|\n234|// backendIDFreeEntries names every exported entry that accepts no\n235|// backend-identity input and constructs no BackendID refusal, with the\n236|// reason. The entry-coverage check requires every derived exported entry\n237|// to appear either here or as some pair's entry, so a new entry that can\n238|// carry an identity fails closed until it gains a battery.\n239|var backendIDFreeEntries = []struct {\n240|\tentry  string\n241|\treason string\n242|}{\n243|\t// Pure predicates over already-built refusals: no identity input.\n244|\t{entry: \"IsProtocolError\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n245|\t{entry: \"IsUnauthorized\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n246|\t{entry: \"IsPreconditionFailed\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n247|\t{entry: \"IsIdempotencyMismatch\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n248|\t{entry: \"IsIncompatibleSchema\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n249|\t{entry: \"IsMismatch\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n250|\t{entry: \"IsCapabilityUnproven\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n251|\t{entry: \"IsIntegrityFailure\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n252|\t{entry: \"IsNotFound\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n253|\t{entry: \"IsAmbiguous\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n254|\t{entry: \"IsUntrusted\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n255|\t{entry: \"IsDrift\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n256|\t{entry: \"IsRestoreMismatch\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n257|\t{entry: \"IsStaleGeneration\", reason: \"predicate over an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n258|\t{entry: \"Error\", reason: \"renders an already-built refusal; takes no backend input\"},\n259|\t// Membership and projection: no BackendID refusal constructed.\n260|\t{entry: \"IDs\", reason: \"reports admitted membership; constructs no refusal\"},\n261|\t{entry: \"DefaultForPlatform\", reason: \"takes a platform, not an identity; its refusals name platforms only\"},\n262|\t{entry: \"Binding\", reason: \"pure projection of an already-validated descriptor; constructs no refusal\"},\n263|\t{entry: \"Has\", reason: \"membership over admitted capabilities; constructs no refusal\"},\n264|\t{entry: \"HasOperation\", reason: \"membership over admitted capabilities; constructs no refusal\"},\n265|\t{entry: \"CapabilitiesForOperation\", reason: \"static capability table lookup; its refusals name operations only\"},\n266|\t{entry: \"CheckOperation\", reason: \"operates on admitted capabilities; its refusals name operations only\"},\n267|\t{entry: \"ClassifyReplication\", reason: \"static replication table lookup; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n268|\t{entry: \"CheckReplicable\", reason: \"operates on member names; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n269|\t// Lifecycle, ledger and attach vocabularies: no identity dimension.\n270|\t{entry: \"ParseInstanceState\", reason: \"lifecycle state vocabulary; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n271|\t{entry: \"ParseOperation\", reason: \"operation vocabulary; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n272|\t{entry: \"ParseSideEffect\", reason: \"side-effect vocabulary; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n273|\t{entry: \"CheckTransition\", reason: \"lifecycle transition over states and operations; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n274|\t{entry: \"CheckErrorAllowed\", reason: \"operation error vocabulary; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n275|\t{entry: \"IdempotencyKey\", reason: \"key-shape validation over operation strings; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n276|\t{entry: \"NewLedger\", reason: \"constructs an empty ledger; constructs no refusal\"},\n277|\t{entry: \"Bind\", reason: \"idempotency-key binding; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n278|\t{entry: \"Replay\", reason: \"idempotency lookup; constructs no refusal\"},\n279|\t{entry: \"Export\", reason: \"ledger serialization; constructs no refusal\"},\n280|\t{entry: \"ImportLedger\", reason: \"ledger image validation; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n281|\t{entry: \"ParseAttachAuthorization\", reason: \"attach authorization document; its members carry no backend identity\"},\n282|\t{entry: \"CheckAttachRequest\", reason: \"attach binding over an already-parsed authorization; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n283|\t{entry: \"CheckAttachResult\", reason: \"attach input binding; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n284|\t{entry: \"CheckEntrypoint\", reason: \"argv and session binding; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n285|\t{entry: \"CheckStatusResult\", reason: \"status identity binding over booleans and digests; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n286|\t// Legacy translation: the refusal names the legacy input shape, and\n287|\t// admitted outputs are closed-map constants, never input bytes.\n288|\t{entry: \"TranslateLegacyBackend\", reason: \"refusal carries no BackendID; output IDs are closed-map constants\"},\n289|\t// Content-addressed helpers: digests and canonical bytes, no identity.\n290|\t{entry: \"GenerationDigest\", reason: \"generation-string digest; takes no backend identity\"},\n291|\t{entry: \"UnsignedEvidenceBytes\", reason: \"canonical evidence bytes; takes no backend identity\"},\n292|\t// I/O helper: plain errors only, never a BackendID refusal.\n293|\t{entry: \"DigestFile\", reason: \"reports I/O failures as plain errors; constructs no BackendID refusal\"},\n294|}\n295|\n296|// backendIDHostileOnlyEntries names exported entries that accept\n297|// identity-influenced input but construct no BackendID refusal of their\n298|// own: hostile input is refused upstream (document admission through\n299|// ParseID, or the ParseID guard for ProjectToLegacy) before any naming\n300|// arm runs. Each carries a hostile battery in\n301|// runBackendIDHostileBatteries but no pair row.\n302|var backendIDHostileOnlyEntries = []string{\n303|\t\"ParseManifest\",\n304|\t\"ParseProbe\",\n305|\t\"ParseEvidence\",\n306|\t\"ParseProviderDescriptor\",\n307|\t\"ProjectToLegacy\",\n308|}\n309|\n310|// backendIDPairKey renders one pair's site identity in the inventory key\n311|// space (line-free, like describeArm).\n312|func backendIDPairKey(file, function, code, detail string, occurrence int) string {\n313|\treturn file + \"|\" + function + \"|\" + code + \"|\" + detail + \"#\" + strconv.Itoa(occurrence)\n314|}\n315|\n316|// deriveBackendIDSites filters the production-derived refusal arms to the\n317|// constructions naming BackendID: the census denominator. The filter reads\n318|// the derived arm's production line through the shared core's scan, so a\n319|// new BackendID arm is derived without anyone remembering this file.\n320|func deriveBackendIDSites(t *testing.T) []refusalArm {\n321|\tt.Helper()\n322|\n323|\tarms := deriveRefusalArms(t)\n324|\tfiles, _ := invcore.MustScanProduction(t, \".\")\n325|\tlinesByFile := make(map[string][]string, len(files))\n326|\tfor _, production := range files {\n327|\t\tlinesByFile[production.Name] = strings.Split(string(production.Source), \"\\n\")\n328|\t}\n329|\tvar sites []refusalArm\n330|\tfor _, arm := range arms {\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
