{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cc91","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07aa8-9772-7fb3-a3d6-487c1d889dad"},"sequence":1187,"recorded_at":1780531400002369,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"a73473aa-819c-46fd-970c-52f307b1d7e0"},"task_id":"a73473aa-819c-46fd-970c-52f307b1d7e0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"a73473aa-819c-46fd-970c-52f307b1d7e0","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-07\n7|\n8|### 1015 — 2okwyf round 3: F2 instrument — Reconcile entry gate plus (site, entry) census, 41/41\n9|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-2okwyf rework (review rev2 CHANGES REQUESTED, blocking F2: site-keyed census read 31/31 while Reconcile echoed at manifest.go:1726/:1762; control plant C1 left the whole suite green). Production: `manifest.go` only — `Reconcile` validates both `manifest.TerminalBackendID` and `probe.TerminalBackendID` through `ParseID` before any check runs (manifest.go:1696/1699; same pattern as CheckVersionTuple/CheckProviderDescriptor). Test: new `internal/terminalbackend/backend_id_entry_census_test.go` (~1300 lines) — derived census keyed by (site, reaching exported entry): 41 pairs + 1 site exemption + 1 pair exemption; every pair carries a guard statement, a hostile-noecho battery through its entry (2 hostile shapes), and a validated fire (12 own fires with recorder attribution + 29 inventoried-witness citations resolved mechanically against DeclaredArmIdentities); entry coverage over all derived exported entries (15 batteried incl. 5 hostile-only + 43 free with reasons). `ParseID` comment rewritten to state what the instrument enforces, nothing beyond.\n10|- FINDING (F2 confirmed pre-fix): hostile structs through production `Reconcile` rendered 305B (`executable substitution`) and 313B (`probe generation binding`) refusals containing the whole string. Red-before: new census `reconcile` battery FAILs (both shapes, both arms); post-fix 41/41 PASS. C1 (ParseID guard out of CheckProviderDescriptor) fails closed on exactly the new test (308B echo) while the rest of the package suite stays green — reproducing the reviewer's plant and proving the instrument, not the old suite, holds the class.\n11|- FINDING (shadowed pair): CheckProviderDescriptor's digest-parse arm is unreachable via AdmitProviderDescriptor (ParseProviderDescriptor's own digest arm fires first) — carried as an executed exempt pair with a shadow pin, not a 42nd pair. Registration.validate's digest-null arm stays the single site exemption (white-box pin executed in-file).\n12|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome-r3.md` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_battery-r3.json` + `TASK-260906-2okwyf_mutants-r3.json` (6 applied/6 killed/0 survived: narrowing 1 N-tb-reconcile-lengthgated with len27-fail/len221-pass split, arm-deletion 2 D-tb-reconcile-entry + D-tb-checkdesc-entry(C1), ordering 1 R-tb-checktuple-order [N2: correctly refiled from narrowing], census-only 1 C-tb-reconcile-deadarm, audit-only 1 S-tb-statusresult-shadow killed only by the full-run audit naming conformance.go:765; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct control rows; masks non-empty; bodies in JSON). N1: anchors re-derived on the final tree (Reconcile guards manifest.go:1696/1699, sites :1741/:1777/:2099/:2102; descriptor guard terminalbackend.go:646; ParseID census note :163). Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, computed AFTER the LOGBOOK append, verified by `ls-tree`.\n13|- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, 0 FAIL), `-race` terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (tb 95.4%, ph 86.0%, pv 97.8%), `go vet ./...` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean.\n14|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n15|\n16|### 0945 — 2okwyf round 2: F1 sibling echo closed at CheckVersionTuple, ParseID comment corrected, 31/31 census\n17|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-2okwyf rework (review rev3 CHANGES REQUESTED, one blocking F1). Production: `terminalbackend.go` only — `CheckVersionTuple` validates `backendID` through `ParseID` before any version arm runs (same pattern as `RequireRestoreBinding`/`CheckProviderDescriptor`); `ParseID` comment rewritten from the false \"like every other BackendID in the package\" to the verifiable per-site invariant (mustParseID at Registration/TrustEntry validate; ParseID at Resolve/RequireRestoreBinding/CheckVersionTuple/CheckProviderDescriptor entries and Manifest/Probe/Evidence admission; constants + validated records at New/RegisterExternal). Test: new `TestCheckVersionTupleRefusesHostileBackendIDWithoutEcho` (3 arms x 2 hostile shapes + valid-ID and ax.evil controls).\n18|- FINDING (F1 confirmed pre-fix): hostile `200xA + ESC[31m + ../../etc/passwd` through production `CheckVersionTuple` rendered a 322-byte refusal containing the whole string at all three arms (BackendID echo + Error() render). Red-before: new test 6/6 FAIL; post-fix 7/7 PASS (exit 0).\n19|- FINDING (census): all 31 BackendID-carrying refusal sites now validated — 27 in terminalbackend.go + 4 in manifest.go (probe arms via ParseProbe admission, manifest arms via ParseManifest admission + Resolve re-validation). Sibling packages measured, NOT changed (sibling suites pin their refusal text: secprim env_test asserts the echo verbatim): environ unknown-member echoes the full wire key (269B refusal, Error()-rendered, LIVE); secprim BuildEnv env-name echoes the full refused name (259B, LIVE); secprim paths truncate to 64 chars via memberErrorTarget (bounded, deliberate); secprim argv echoes positions only (clean); provhost Error() never echoes (static messages; identifiers travel in Details, inert + 16KiB ValidateDetails cap). The two LIVE sites are stated bounds with entry points, escaping content, and owner (sibling-suite pins) — follow-up leaves, not this diff.\n20|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome-r2.md` + `battery_2okwyf_r2.json` (5 applied/5 killed/0 survived: narrowing 2 incl. length-gated + reorder, arm-deletion 1, census-only 1, audit-only 1 naming terminalbackend.go:651; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct rows; masks 15/243/665 all non-empty; mutant bodies in JSON). Round-1 battery anchors all still present (grep-verified); round-1 outcome/battery resources stand for unchanged code. Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, detached-index write-tree AFTER the LOGBOOK append.\n21|- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (all ok), `-race` terminalbackend exit 0, `-cover` exit 0 (tb 95.1%, ph 86.0%, pv 97.8%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean.\n22|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n23|\n24|### 0839 — 2okwyf: A5/A7/A8/A9/F-B1 closed (cross-package agreement, trust asymmetry, three nits, digit-guard sentence)\n25|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-2okwyf, fourth leaf of STORY-260905-3t31e9. Production: `terminalbackend.go` (ParseID grammar arm drops BackendID echo; DigestFile §6.5/§7.1 asymmetry note), `provider.go` (trustCandidate §7.1/§6.5 mirror note), `provhost/probe.go` (decodeValidatedProbe single-decode split; RequireCapability consumes validated members), `provhost/protocol.go` (parseMajor leading-zero stated bound). Tests: new `provhost/profile_agreement_test.go` (order-sensitive cross-package equality), `TestParseIDGrammarRefusalEchoesNothing`, `TestParseMajorLeadingZeroIsClassifiedAsForeign`, `TestDecodeValidatedProbeHandsUsableMembersToRequireCapability`; one false sentence corrected in `digit_guard_census_test.go`.\n26|- FINDING (A5 premise narrowed): a direct set-equality pin already exists (`TestSixProviderSetMatchesDiscoveryRegistry`, story-2 base) — the live hole was ORDER agreement only. Reorder mutant on either side alone leaves the whole old suite green and reddens only the new order pin (M-xprov-reorder: census 27 ran SURVIVED, behav 2 ran KILLED by the new test).\n27|- FINDING (F-B1 sentence false as stated): pure named-const digit chain prunes silently — additive plant in `provhost/protocol.go` left both packages green (full suites) — while a mixed chain (named leaf + literal leaf) fails as unclassifiable (`mixes digit comparisons with unrelated comparisons`). First mixed probe passed vacuously on a wrong `-run` mask (matched only the unit test, census never ran); re-ran with `TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard` non-empty. Sentence corrected to the precise split; absence re-verified by AST scan (0 digit-valued named constants, 0 such comparisons).\n28|- FINDING (parseMajor strictness not free): rejecting leading zeros spells `== '0'`, which the digit-guard census rejects as unclassifiable (verified: strict mutant kills `TestDigitCensusCoversEveryLeafGuard` with ran=1 plus the provhost inventory with an unwitnessed parse arm) — so the bound close (classify-only, both arms refuse, gate admits exactly \"2.0.0\") is the correct one, pinned by `TestParseMajorLeadingZeroIsClassifiedAsForeign`.\n29|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-2okwyf_outcome.md` + `battery_2okwyf.json` (9 applied/9 killed/0 survived; narrowing 4, arm-deletion 2, census-only 1, audit-only 1 [leaf3 S-tb-shadow re-verified: census 15 + behav 229 SURVIVED, audit 658 KILLED naming conformance.go:713,:716], agreement 1; NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct) attached as task resources. AC 4/4 rows driven. Candidate tree OID in the outcome doc, verified by `ls-tree` after every artifact write.\n30|- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok, 0 FAIL), `-race` exit 0 (23 ok), `-cover` exit 0 (provhost 86.0%, provider 97.8%, terminalbackend 95.0%), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows go vet` exit 0, `go build` + `GOOS=windows go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok, catalog current, cigate contracts 6/6 + claims 6/6, fuzz smoke 13/13.\n31|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n32|\n33|### 0715 — v8heil round 2: site-recording seam closes the sibling-swallow class (F1/F2), all six findings fixed\n34|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-v8heil rework (review rev2 CHANGES REQUESTED). Production seam in 4 files: `recordRefusal` hook (nil in prod) + `refuse` funnel (`//go:noinline`), hook calls in `mismatchf`/`integrityFailure`, 89 `&Error{}` literals routed through `refuse` same-line. Tests: new `refusal_site_audit_test.go` (TestMain exercised-line audit, row↔line mapping, skip pin, refuse-alias pins), line-carrying derivation with refuse-wrap enforcement, derived shadow-cover analysis replacing the 19 hand pairs, corrected N-R1 bound, dead loop deleted.\n35|- FINDING (measured): pair-proves do not attribute — P8 plant left derivation identical + all 184 witnesses green; the audit kills it naming `conformance.go:713, :716`. The audit also caught a REAL pre-existing swallow on first run (`descriptor.go:123` never fired; #2 witness proved via sibling #1) — fixed as a witness (rename-away), not a bound.\n36|- FINDING: clause sharing recomputed identically (62/184, 20 clauses, largest x11); death residual now 0/184. Stated remainder: rows bind to lines, witnesses do not (complementary swap invisible; shared with provider/provhost by construction).\n37|- FINDING: F3's \"no strconv site\" was false — `provhost/opdecode.go rawUint53` exists, pinned by `count_overflow` (battery row B- reproduces the narrow-to-maxUint53+1 plant/kill).\n38|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-v8heil_outcome-r2.md` + batteries (`battery_tb_r2` 8/8 incl. audit-only S-tb-shadow, `battery_ph_strconv` B-, re-ran core/pv/ph/x green; 19 applied/19 killed/0 survived + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL distinct) attached as task resources. Census: tb 210/210 lines (26 bound, 14 codes), ph 167/15, pv 18/3. AC 4/4 rows, refusals 369/395 driven + 26 bound. Candidate tree `9d7eaa4d…` verified by `ls-tree` + `hash-object` (11/11 MATCH).\n39|- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (23 ok), `-race` exit 0 (23 ok), `-cover` exit 0 (70.2/86.0/97.8/95.0), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok, catalog current, cigate pass.\n40|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n(more lines below)"}}}
