{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd91","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07aa8-9772-7fb3-a3d6-487c1d889dad"},"sequence":1315,"recorded_at":1780531400002625,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a1248ce4-fca2-4c19-838c-c9c2fefd9f3b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"408eff1d-3777-433c-ba07-66fdb2ddb16a"},"task_id":"408eff1d-3777-433c-ba07-66fdb2ddb16a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"408eff1d-3777-433c-ba07-66fdb2ddb16a","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-37-1\",\n  \"command\": \"python3 .temp/TASK-260906-2okwyf/mutate_base.py .temp/TASK-260906-2okwyf/muts_r4.json .temp/TASK-260906-2okwyf/battery_r4.json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"\\nimport sys, json\\nfor line in sys.stdin:\\n    line = line.strip()\\n    if line.startswith('SUMMARY'):\\n        print(line)\\n        continue\\n    r = json.loads(line)\\n    for m in ('census','behav','audit'):\\n        if m in r and isinstance(r[m], dict):\\n            r[m] = {k: (v[:2] if isinstance(v, list) else v) for k, v in r[m].items()}\\n    print(json.dumps(r))\\n\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Run round-4 mutation battery\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"id\\\": \\\"N-tb-sitefilter-linegated\\\", \\\"class\\\": \\\"narrowing\\\", \\\"expect\\\": \\\"narrowing: the site filter stays but is keyed on the arm's source line again (the retired round-3 spelling), admitting exactly the multi-line-composite-literal subclass. Killed by the new synthetic-multiline test; inventory census SURVIVES (no refuse line added or removed).\\\", \\\"census\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"SURVIVED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 15, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"    refusal_site_audit_test.go:161: refusal-site audit domain: 210 derived lines, 26 bound-exempt, 14 wire codes\\\"]}, \\\"behav\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 32, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"--- FAIL: TestBackendIDSiteFilterSeesMultilineSpelling (0.06s)\\\", \\\"FAIL\\\"]}, \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"killers\\\": [\\\"behav\\\"]}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"D-tb-sitefilter-flag\\\", \\\"class\\\": \\\"arm-deletion\\\", \\\"expect\\\": \\\"arm-deletion: the backendID flag read is gone, so the denominator is always empty and the filter fails itself. Killed everywhere (zero-sites Fatalf fails the binary); the inventory census fails too because every mask shares the process.\\\", \\\"census\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"SURVIVED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 15, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"    refusal_site_audit_test.go:161: refusal-site audit domain: 210 derived lines, 26 bound-exempt, 14 wire codes\\\"]}, \\\"behav\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 3, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"--- FAIL: TestBackendIDSiteFilterSeesMultilineSpelling (0.01s)\\\", \\\"--- FAIL: TestBackendIDEntryCensus (0.01s)\\\"]}, \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"killers\\\": [\\\"behav\\\"]}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"N-tb-entryindex-samekind\\\", \\\"class\\\": \\\"narrowing\\\", \\\"expect\\\": \\\"narrowing: the collision gate stays but only reports receiverless pairs, admitting exactly the func-vs-method and method-vs-method subclasses. Killed by the new synthetic-collision test; inventory census SURVIVES (no entry added or removed).\\\", \\\"census\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"SURVIVED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 15, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"    refusal_site_audit_test.go:161: refusal-site audit domain: 210 derived lines, 26 bound-exempt, 14 wire codes\\\"]}, \\\"behav\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 32, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"    backend_id_entry_census_test.go:510: synthetic bare-name collision absorbed without a trace: got [], want a CensusCollisionProbe collision\\\", \\\"--- FAIL: TestExportedEntryDerivationFailsClosedOnCollision (0.02s)\\\"]}, \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"killers\\\": [\\\"behav\\\"]}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"D-tb-entryindex-enforce\\\", \\\"class\\\": \\\"arm-deletion\\\", \\\"expect\\\": \\\"arm-deletion: the fail-closed enforcement is dropped (collisions collected but ignored). SURVIVES on the live tree: zero repeats among today's 59 bare names, so nothing observes the dropped check. Observable only with a colliding entry: the P2 plant run stays GREEN under this mutant and goes RED under the fixed gate.\\\", \\\"census\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"SURVIVED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 15, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"    refusal_site_audit_test.go:161: refusal-site audit domain: 210 derived lines, 26 bound-exempt, 14 wire codes\\\"]}, \\\"behav\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"SURVIVED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 32, \\\"evidence\\\": []}, \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"SURVIVED\\\", \\\"killers\\\": []}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"C-tb-multiline-deadarm\\\", \\\"class\\\": \\\"census-only\\\", \\\"expect\\\": \\\"census-only: new derived BackendID arm in the multi-line spelling, dead by construction (a condition no input satisfies), so no behavior change. Killed by the inventory census (unregistered arm) AND by the entry-census mapping (unpaired site); no behavioral probe observes it.\\\", \\\"census\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 15, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"--- FAIL: TestDeclaredRefusalArmsAreAllDerived (0.01s)\\\", \\\"--- FAIL: TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllDeclared (0.01s)\\\"]}, \\\"behav\\\": {\\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"ran\\\": 32, \\\"evidence\\\": [\\\"--- FAIL: TestBackendIDEntryCensus (0.01s)\\\", \\\"FAIL\\\"]}, \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"KILLED\\\", \\\"killers\\\": [\\\"census\\\", \\\"behav\\\"]}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"X-control-notapplied\\\", \\\"class\\\": \\\"control\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"NOT_APPLIED\\\", \\\"detail\\\": \\\"anchor occurs 0 times\\\"}\\n{\\\"id\\\": \\\"X-control-compilefail\\\", \\\"class\\\": \\\"control\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"COMPILE_FAIL\\\", \\\"detail\\\": [\\\"# github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provider\\\", \\\"# [github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/provider]\\\", \\\"vet: internal/provider/provider.go:366:20: expected ')', found '{' (and 2 more errors)\\\"]}\\nSUMMARY {\\\"KILLED\\\": 4, \\\"SURVIVED\\\": 1, \\\"NOT_APPLIED\\\": 1, \\\"COMPILE_FAIL\\\": 1}\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4050,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1013,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
